{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three,\n    while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a copy of the original list to modify.\n    result_list = list(l)\n\n    # Collect elements at indices divisible by three and their original positions.\n    elements_to_sort = []\n    indices_to_replace = []\n\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            elements_to_sort.append(l[i])\n            indices_to_replace.append(i)\n\n    # Sort the collected elements in ascending order.\n    elements_to_sort.sort()\n\n    # Replace elements in the result list with the sorted elements.\n    for i, original_index in enumerate(indices_to_replace):\n        result_list[original_index] = elements_to_sort[i]\n\n    return result_list"}
