{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there are three distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n    It sorts the list and uses a two-pointer approach for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # Trusting input 'l' is a list of integers as per critical requirements.\n    # Sort the list to use the two-pointer approach.\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Skip duplicate elements for 'i' to avoid redundant checks.\n        if i > 0 and sorted_l[i] == sorted_l[i-1]:\n            continue\n\n        left = i + 1\n        right = n - 1\n\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = sorted_l[i] + sorted_l[left] + sorted_l[right]\n\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else: # current_sum > 0\n                right -= 1\n    return False"}
