{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result = \"\"\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        result = str(remainder) + result\n        current_x //= base\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Use dynamic programming (tabulation) to avoid recursion.\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    dp[1] = 0\n    dp[2] = 2\n    dp[3] = 0\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2] + dp[i-3] + dp[i-4]\n\n    return dp[n]"}
