{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    This function efficiently calculates fib4(n) in O(n) time and O(1) space, avoiding recursion.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp stores the last four computed Fib4 numbers: [fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1)]\n    dp = [0, 0, 2, 0] # Represents fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = dp[0] + dp[1] + dp[2] + dp[3]\n        # Shift the window to keep only the last four values\n        dp.pop(0)\n        dp.append(next_fib4)\n    \n    return dp[3]"}
